# model-routing.env — per-intent model routing (PXC-30 / hardening 13)
#
# Plain operator-editable config: `intent = provider/model` (one per line).
# Lines starting with # are comments; malformed lines are ignored. Editing
# this file takes effect on the NEXT message — no bridge reload needed
# (the bridge re-reads it per request). Removing the file disables routing.
#
# Intents the bridge classifies: work | research | chat | default
#   - work:     build/fix/ship phrasing (debug, implement, refactor, ...)
#   - research: explicit research/lookup phrasing (research, riset, ...)
#   - default:  everything else (quick chat) — also the fallback for any
#               unrecognized intent. Keep it = the profile default model
#               (paci-x settings.json: vikey/glm-5.3-flash).
#   - chat:     reserved bucket (same model as default for now)
# Alternate (failover) lines: `alternate:<intent> = provider/model`.
# On a provider error the same request is retried once on the alternate
# and logged as model_failover. Omit them to disable failover.
#
# Available vikey models (2026-09-06): glm/glm-5.3-flash,
# openai/gpt-5.6-luna, openai/gpt-5.6-sol.

work = openai/gpt-5.6-sol
research = openai/gpt-5.6-luna
chat = vikey/glm-5.3-flash
default = vikey/glm-5.3-flash

alternate:work = vikey/glm-5.3-flash
alternate:research = vikey/glm-5.3-flash
alternate:default = openai/gpt-5.6-luna
